# Project outputs (anchored to root - does NOT match src/wildfire_nowcast/data)
# NOTE the `/*` form on /data: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIR is
# excluded, so `/data/` + `!/data/norm_stats.json` would silently not work.
/data/*
!/data/norm_stats.json
/outputs/
*.mp4

# `runs/` is 92 MB of evidence and stays out of the public tree, EXCEPT for the
# twelve artifacts that tracked public source cites BY NAME. Twelve of twelve
# were unopenable to a reader, including `s1.json` and `e1.json`, the two
# headline results: source that cites evidence the repository does not contain
# reads as fabricated provenance even though every file is real and present.
# They total 4,338,332 bytes, 4.5% of the directory. Tracking them also PINS
# them, so a silent regeneration becomes a diff.
#
# THE CLASS IS ENUMERATED BY `tools/cited_runs.py`, NOT BY A PATTERN TYPED HERE.
# The list below was first built from `runs/[A-Za-z0-9_]*.json`, which cannot
# match a subdirectory or a non-json extension and therefore found twelve of
# twenty-one. `tools/cited_runs.py` walks every tracked file for every `runs/`
# token, resolves it on disk and classifies it, so a citation cannot be missed
# for having the wrong shape. `tests/test_cited_runs.py` runs it on every commit
# and fails when a new citation appears with nowhere to resolve.
#
# THE FIVE `_*.py` ARE THE IMPORTANT HALF. They are the code that produced
# published numbers, cited from public source and, until now, absent from the
# repository. That is the C0 breach STATE.md records, not a size problem: 48 KB.
#
# DECLARED EXEMPTION, WITH ITS REASON. The four `baselines-*/results.json` are
# cited and stay out. They carry 120 occurrences of an internal coordination role
# name inside `note` strings that the scoring code emitted at run time, across
# two distinct sentences. They are evidence and may not be edited to look
# better; tracking them unedited would publish those 120 and require a
# never-retireable entry in the burn-down list in `tests/test_hygiene.py`, which
# is an exemption wearing a burn-down list's clothes. The tell count is pinned in
# `tests/test_cited_runs.py`, so this reason fails the day it stops being true.
# Their 12.7 MB is a secondary objection, not the reason.
#
# NOTE the `/*` form, for the same reason `/data/*` uses it above: git cannot
# re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded. Adding a file here is a
# deliberate edit, which is the intended cost.
/runs/*
!/runs/e1.json
!/runs/m6_innovation_autocorr.json
!/runs/m7_offstate_optimum.json
!/runs/m7_spatial_lever.json
!/runs/m8_partition_probe.json
!/runs/m8_transfer_probe.json
!/runs/m9_scaling.json
!/runs/m12_frontier.json
!/runs/s1.json
!/runs/s1_rows_a_s1.json
!/runs/u0.json
!/runs/u0b.json
!/runs/_m9_response.py
!/runs/_m9_scaling.py
!/runs/_m10_bitidentity.py
!/runs/_s1_bitidentity.py
!/runs/_s1_score.py

# Generated figures and the review page (32.8 MB, rebuilt by sim/review.py).
# WARNING: these are only regenerable together with /runs/, which is ALSO
# ignored - so a fresh clone cannot reproduce them. See STATE.md "PROVENANCE
# GAP": run records are the evidence behind every gate verdict and are
# currently unversioned. Needs a decision (git-lfs or an external archive).
/reports/

